{"uid":"35b40f54a5d720e6","name":"test_C3_dependent_retake_waits_on_both_cure_and_freeze","fullName":"tests.test_cure_freeze_dependent_reselection_task008#test_C3_dependent_retake_waits_on_both_cure_and_freeze","historyId":"fc6c6baf23ec40086a98a19b13f1561f","time":{"start":1791919946865,"stop":1791919946872,"duration":7},"description":"`030` is a dependent re-take: it names the freeze (`020`) in its own\n    `dependsOn`, and carries a `priority` (99) that would beat every other\n    pending candidate outright if the scheduler only looked at priority.\n    Walk the chain stage by stage:\n\n    1. cure pending, freeze pending (now depending on the cure), dependent\n       pending (depending on the freeze) -> the scheduler must pick the\n       cure, not the high-priority dependent.\n    2. cure done, freeze still pending -> the scheduler must pick the\n       freeze, not the dependent -- the freeze prerequisite alone still\n       blocks the dependent even though its own cure prerequisite cleared.\n    3. cure done, freeze done -> only then is the dependent selectable.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>030</code> is a dependent re-take: it names the freeze (<code>020</code>) in its own<br />\n<code>dependsOn</code>, and carries a <code>priority</code> (99) that would beat every other<br />\npending candidate outright if the scheduler only looked at priority.<br />\nWalk the chain stage by stage:</p>\n<pre><code>1. cure pending, freeze pending (now depending on the cure), dependent\n   pending (depending on the freeze) -&gt; the scheduler must pick the\n   cure, not the high-priority dependent.\n2. cure done, freeze still pending -&gt; the scheduler must pick the\n   freeze, not the dependent -- the freeze prerequisite alone still\n   blocks the dependent even though its own cure prerequisite cleared.\n3. cure done, freeze done -&gt; only then is the dependent selectable.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed"